      },
      "lineNbr": 190,
      "author": {
        "id": 1141739
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-23T13:50:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "by the way, how does internal keyboard on non-tablet devices handle this?",
      "parentUuid": "ca142d72_c71452cd",
      "revId": "6119579ffd4ba70656d4f501d1b0d44658f408da",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7cf67296_4e3af042",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/usb_hid_keyboard.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 190,
      "author": {
        "id": 1289152
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-23T19:00:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Internal keyboards don\u0027t actually use HID, they either use the AT keyboard protocol (on x86) or I2C (on ARM) instead. Sadly neither of those have a way to report what keys are supported, so in those cases we can only determine the presence of number pads etc. by looking up the board name from VPD.",
      "parentUuid": "4703619b_b57fecdc",
      "revId": "6119579ffd4ba70656d4f501d1b0d44658f408da",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a6ebf9d9_6cde6c55",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/usb_hid_keyboard.c",
